TASK
Create {{ batch_size }} contrastive groups.

Each group contains:
- ONE sentence ({{ min_len }}–{{ max_len }} words)
- TWO conversational contexts for the same sentence
- Each context forces stress on a DIFFERENT single word

OUTPUT FORMAT (JSON)
{
  "groups": [
    {
      "sentence": "...",
      "variations": [
        {"context": "...", "stressed_word": "..."},
        {"context": "...", "stressed_word": "..."}
      ]
    }
  ]
}

PLANNING CONSTRAINTS (must be obeyed)

PLAN ASSIGNMENTS
Variation 1:
- POS={{ pos_plan }}
- MODE={{ mode_plan }}
- CTX={{ ctx_plan }}

Variation 2:
- Must stress the other candidate word.


STYLE AND CONTENT
- Context length: {{ min_len }}–{{ max_len }} words
- Sentence: simple, spoken, one clause, max one comma
- Vocabulary: CEFR B1
- Tone: {{ selected_style }}
- Topics: {{ topic_hint }}
- Micro-style: {{ micro_hint }}
- Banned patterns: {{ ban_hint }}
- Context bans: {{ ctx_ban_hint }}

DIVERSITY
- Do not reuse the same context opening (first 3 words) across items.
- Do not reuse fixed phrasing templates across the batch.

FINAL SELF-CHECK (do silently)
- Does the context force the stressed word as the only correction?
- Is the other candidate still plausible under a different context?
If not, rewrite before outputting JSON.
